<http://data.silknow.org/object/eb2bb488-4aad-35b4-be01-479ad1936f1a>
        a                              ecrm:E22_Man-Made_Object ;
        rdfs:comment                   "1800s, Persian; Flowers"@en , "Description: Dress fabric of woven silk and metal thread; with weft floats on the back. Gold ground with rows of botehs facing the opposite direction in alternate rows.  The metal thread is silver-strip open S-wound on a yellow silk core and is the foundation weft.  The warp is orange silk. It is a loose sateen weave.  Each boteh is plump with red roots, a dark outline, dark green leaves, a central white blossom and red and light blue flowers. At the top of the piece is a band of red silk which marks a loom end or piece end. There are places in which red silk has been used instead of orange in the weft."@en ;
        ecrm:P138i_has_representation  <http://data.silknow.org/image/8acd358f-2261-3f6a-9af5-533f94a527c9> ;
        ecrm:P3_has_note               "Description: Dress fabric of woven silk and metal thread; with weft floats on the back. Gold ground with rows of botehs facing the opposite direction in alternate rows.  The metal thread is silver-strip open S-wound on a yellow silk core and is the foundation weft.  The warp is orange silk. It is a loose sateen weave.  Each boteh is plump with red roots, a dark outline, dark green leaves, a central white blossom and red and light blue flowers. At the top of the piece is a band of red silk which marks a loom end or piece end. There are places in which red silk has been used instead of orange in the weft."@en , "1800s, Persian; Flowers"@en ;
